From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron <aaronmedeiros@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] colorspace: preserve chroma during inverse tone mapping

The ordinary conservative ITP hull correction contains I_in / I_out.  That
is useful while compressing brightness, but necessarily desaturates every
inverse expansion even when the expanded color remains representable.

Keep source ITP P/T during a genuine inverse expansion and leave the existing
output-gamut mapper responsible for colors that actually cross the target
boundary.  Normal tone mapping and non-expanding inverse requests are
unchanged.
---
 src/shaders/colorspace.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/shaders/colorspace.c b/src/shaders/colorspace.c
index bfc92844..00000000 100644
--- a/src/shaders/colorspace.c
+++ b/src/shaders/colorspace.c
@@ -3020,6 +3020,8 @@ void pl_shader_color_map_ex(pl_shader sh, const struct pl_color_map_params *para
         params->ambient_gamma > 0.0f ? params->ambient_gamma : 1.0f;
     const bool ambient_active = fabsf(ambient_gamma - 1.0f) > 1e-6f;
     const bool base_need_tone_map = !pl_tone_map_params_noop(&tone);
+    const bool inverse_expansion = params->inverse_tone_mapping &&
+        tone.output_max > tone.input_max + 1e-6f;
     bool need_tone_map = base_need_tone_map || ambient_active;
     bool need_gamut_map = !pl_gamut_map_params_noop(&gamut);
 
@@ -3291,11 +3294,15 @@ void pl_shader_color_map_ex(pl_shader sh, const struct pl_color_map_params *para
         // Avoid raising saturation excessively when raising brightness, and
         // also desaturate when reducing brightness greatly to account for the
         // reduction in gamut volume.
-        if (!metric_active ||
+        // A genuine inverse expansion is different: reducing P/T by I_in/I_out
+        // visibly desaturates colors that remain inside the larger target
+        // gamut. Preserve P/T there and let the output-gamut stage constrain
+        // only colors that actually cross its boundary.
+        if (!inverse_expansion && (!metric_active ||
             params->tone_mapping_metric == PL_TONE_MAP_METRIC_BT2020_ITP ||
             params->tone_mapping_metric == PL_TONE_MAP_METRIC_BT2020_ADAPTIVE ||
             params->tone_mapping_metric == PL_TONE_MAP_METRIC_MAXRGB_ITP ||
-            params->tone_mapping_metric == PL_TONE_MAP_METRIC_MAXRGB_ADAPTIVE) {
+            params->tone_mapping_metric == PL_TONE_MAP_METRIC_MAXRGB_ADAPTIVE)) {
             GLSL("vec2 hull = vec2(i_orig, ipt.x);                       \n"
                  "hull = ((hull - 6.0) * hull + 9.0) * hull;             \n"
                  "float chroma_scale = min(i_orig / max(ipt.x, 1e-6),   \n"
 
